1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,880
The problem is that people only ever see the final result.

2
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:11,300
A BASE jumper may have done the jump 20 or 30 times before being able to fly the line precisely.

3
00:00:12,180 --> 00:00:16,100
But they only post the best line they have ever flown.

4
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:19,660
The one where they flew closer to the terrain than ever before.

5
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:25,460
And that's problematic because someone watching the video might think,

6
00:00:26,180 --> 00:00:27,640
they did it on their first attempt.

7
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:32,400
If you then try to repeat that line, you might overlook all the preparation

8
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:37,360
and attempt to fly that exact line on your very first jump.

9
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:44,320
Personally, I sometimes struggle with the fact that people only post their highlights

10
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:46,940
and not the process that got them there.

11
00:00:47,940 --> 00:00:52,260
Because I think many people, especially younger jumpers who grew up with social media,

12
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:57,380
would benefit from seeing the process behind those highlights.